  "content": "Indu becomes first Nepali woman to score 1,000 runs in T20I cricket\nOnlinekhabar\nTuesday, October 7, 2025\n0\nComments\nKathmandu, October 7\nNepal women’s cricket team captain Indu Barma has become the first Nepali woman cricketer to score 1,000 runs in T20 International cricket.\nIndu reached the milestone during Nepal’s victory against Malaysia on Tuesday, where she remained unbeaten on 48 runs.\nShe has scored her runs at an average of 18 and has hit one half-century so far, with her highest individual score being 55 runs.\nReact to this post\nHot Topics\nNepal\nElection Commission\ncricket\nshare market\nroad\nGen Z\nMaitighar\nConversation\nNew\nOld\nPopular\nAdd Comment\nLogin to comment\nRemenber me\nForgot password?\nLogin\nNot have account yet?\nSignup Now\nOr use Social Media?\nGoogle\nFacebook\nTwitter\nForgot Password?\nSend Password Reset Link\nBack\nRelated News\nMost Read\nHighways blocked nationwide as heavy rainfall disrupts travel\nFlood risks in Kathmandu, KMC launches helpline service\nCAA publishes domestic airfare rates, Kathmandu–Dhangadhi at Rs 17,579\nUAE introduces new rules for Visit Visa Sponsorship\nDeath toll from landslides and floods rises to 52 across Nepal\nSubscribe to our newsletter\nSubscribe to Onlinekhabar English to get notified of exclusive news stories.\nEditor's Pick\nEditor's Pick\n4 government buildings, including Supreme Court, declared unfit for use\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nCharred body found at Koteshwor Bhatbhateni, Gen-Z protest death toll rises to 74\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nNo consensus on Hami Nepal’s claim of leading the Gen-Z movement\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nDecades-old irrigation projects stall as Madhesh faces drought, food crisis looms\n3 months ago\nEditor's Pick\nNepal’s farming crisis: When plans stay on paper and fields suffer\n3 months ago\nAlso Read\nOpinion\nGen Z movement in Nepal at a crossroads: Between reform, revolt and reflection\n3 hours ago\nSociety\nDiversions built at 3 sections of BP Highway\n3 hours ago\nBlog\nHow Gen Z turned a hashtag into a revolution in Nepal\n3 hours ago\nPolitics\nElection Commission invites parties for talks on upcoming House election\n20 hours ago\nSociety\nSeven charged in Pokhara Lichhibari land scam involving former ministers and officials\n20 hours ago",
